SOHO Small Office Network – Packet Tracer Project
In this project, I designed and implemented a Small Office/Home Office (SOHO) network using Cisco Packet Tracer. The goal was to build a secure, scalable, and functional network that provides LAN connectivity, wireless access, automatic IP assignment (DHCP), and controlled internet access using NAT and ACL-based firewall rules.

Objectives
Provide connectivity between wired and wireless devices
Automatically assign IP addresses using DHCP
Enable internet access using NAT (PAT)
Secure the internal network from external access using ACLs
Simulate a real-world office network environment

Network Components
🔹 Core Devices
Cisco Router (ISP Simulation)
Firewall Router (Internal Gateway + NAT + DHCP)
Cisco 2960 Switch
Wireless Access Point
🔹 End Devices
PCs (wired users)
Laptop (wireless user)
